OL,5,G1930 Radio 3 in Concert
OL,6,     FThe celebrated Canadian pianist
OL,7,     FAngela Hewitt plays fortepiano
OL,8,     Fwith the Dunedin Consort in two
OL,9,     Fcontrasting concertos by CPE Bach
OL,10,     Fand Mozart, plus Haydn's 6th
OL,11,     FSymphony, 'Le matin'.
OL,12,G2145 The Essay: Coltrane's Sound
OL,13,     FComposer and minimalism pioneer
OL,14,     FSteve Reich remembers the music of
OL,15,     Fjazz musician John Coltrane.
OL,16,     FPresented by Ashley Kahn.
OL,17,G2200 Night Tracks
OL,18,     FSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,19,     Fadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,20,     Ffor late-night listening, from
OL,21,     Fclassical to contemporary and
OL,22,     Feverything in between.
